doom-modeline is a fancy and fast Emacs mode line with a minimalist
design, originally written for Doom Emacs.  It shows file and buffer
state, version control status, error and warning counts from flymake
and flycheck, the current major mode with icons from nerd-icons, and
optional segments for modal editing state, LSP and debugger status,
window and workspace numbers, input method, battery, remote host, and
notifications from GitHub, mail and IRC.  Nearly every segment can be
toggled or customized, and the mode line height is configurable.
